* On the server nginx listens on port 8100 and presents a wildcard cert for `*.puppet.gigya.net`, signed by Devops-CA; nginx checks the client cert.

The page then shows the relevant nginx proxy snippet from `/etc/nginx/conf.d/proxy.conf`:

```
server {
    listen      8100 ssl;
    server_name mgla-puppet1;

    proxy_next_upstream error timeout http_502;

    ssl_certificate      /etc/nginx/certs/wild.puppet.gigya.net.crt;
    ssl_certificate_key  /etc/nginx/certs/wild.puppet.gigya.net.key;
    ssl_client_certificate /etc/nginx/certs/wild.puppet.gigya.net.crt;
    ssl_session_ticket_key shared:SSL:1m;
    ssl_session_timeout 5m;
    ssl_verify_client optional;
    ...
}
```

It explains `ssl_client_certificate` holds the file used to verify clients, `ssl_verify_client optional` is used because other non-Puppet resources share port 8100, X-Client-Verify is used to let the server know the agent is validated and nginx then adds two headers and proxies to backend1, and that nginx forwards to Varnish on localhost 6081.

